item.description:
drafting&hellip;
2025-05-10 Simple Made Easy, Richard Hickey talk, takeaways,
Listening to this presentation, from the frame of why do codebases get difficult to change , but also how you plan changes you want to make on the scale of a &ldquo;story&rdquo; or &ldquo;bug&rdquo; and also just a &ldquo;day&rdquo; and even a single block of time you have for a particular story. The definition of simple as simplex as one interleave and less simplex as more &ldquo;concepts&rdquo; that are taken together to be more &ldquo;complex&rdquo;.

a bit tricky, not super intuitive in the docs, but I finally found how to builf a typesense query to do what I had previously done with postgres, that is, first constrain by postgis distance and then order by cosine distance.
with a text_embedding column that embeds a text column, and lat lng available as well, flattened on the same collection, it is possible to query like so,
{	&#34;q&#34;: query, &#34;query_by&#34;: &#34;text_embedding&#34;, &#34;filter_by&#34;: f&#34;location:({lat}, {lng}, {radius_km} km)&#34;, &#34;sort_by&#34;: &#34;_vector_distance:asc&#34;, &#34;exclude_fields&#34;: &#34;text_embedding&#34;, &#39;page&#39;: 1, &#39;per_page&#39;: 100 }
